    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.indentscope\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nIf the buffer direction is set to right to left with `:set rightleft`, when the animation starts, the text disappears.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.9.4\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1- open any file with some indentation and mini.align activated\r\n2- :set rightleft\r\n3- move the cursor to a new block of text\r\n4. the block starts to disappear\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nindented blocks starts to disappear in rightleft mode.",
    "closed_at": "2024-03-29T12:35:07Z",
