    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nI indeed can reproduce on Neovim 0.9.5, but it seems to be fixed on current [Nightly version 0.10](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/releases/tag/nightly).\r\n\r\nThe reason this happens is the way the line is drawn to be more robust against left-right window scroll and it indeed implicitly assumes that there is an empty space to the left of it. As it is quite a fundamental implementation detail, I'm afraid my only suggestion would be to use Nightly for this (or wait until 0.10 release, which *should* be soon-ish enough).\r\n\r\nClosing as fixed on latest Neovim version.",
